Restores §7.5 step 3 as it was before draft 54 (9c0f69e): a source that
answers `NotAvailable` is removed from the want instead of being refused
for an hour, so only its own announcement of the wanted content makes it
a source again, and a want whose every source refused and none announces
stays without a source for good (DESIGN.md §7.5 step 3). No seed fails
with this patch in 44,300 (0 to 1,999 and the 76,000, 86,000 and 96,000
slices at the defaults, and 0 to 19,999 in two-node and in three-node
worlds at 200 steps): with the serve-mismatch observation in place, a
source that can serve again says so. The rule's unit tests stand in for a
pinned seed.

